1,2 $Stipe with persistent flaring membranous ring.
1,6 $ Stipe with evanescent floccose-scaly ring zone.
2,3 $ Basidiospores 4-5 x 3-3.5 µm, amyloid, broadly ellipsoid to ellipsoid.
2,4 $ Basidiospores longer (>5 µm) than above.
3,0 $ Pileus and slipe white with greyish pink or vinaceous linge.3. $ Cystoderma carcharias
3,0 $ Pileus rusly (rarely médium brown or ochre).  4. $ Cystoderma fallax
4,0 $ Pileus ochre, ring narrow. Basidiospores 5-6 x 2.5-3.5 µm, oblong.  5. $ Cystoderma intermedium
4,5 $ Pileus brown, basidiospores wider (>3.5 µm) than above, broadly ellipsoid to ellipsoid.
5,0 $ Pileus fulvous brown. Basidiospores 5-7 x 3.5-4.5 µm. 11. $ Cystoderma tuomikoskii
5,0 $ Pileus rusty brown. Basidiospores 6-10 x 4-6 µm. 2. $ Cystoderma arcticum
6,7 $ Basidiospores amyloid.
6,11 $ Basidiospores inamyloid.
7,0 $ Basidiocarp white. Basidiospores 5.5-8.0 x 3.0-4.5 µm, oblong to fusiform.8. $ Cystoderma niveum
7,8 $ Basidiocarp coloured.
8,9 $ Pileus yellowish ochre.
8,10 $ Pileus brownish ochre to dark brown.
9,0 $ Lamellae white. Basidiospores 5-6.5 x 2.5-3.5 µm, ellipsoid to oblong. Arthrospores laeking or rare bencath pellipellis context.1. $ Cystoderma amianthinum
9,0 $ Lamellae yellowish. Basidiospores 6-7.5 x 3-4 µm, oblong to fusiform. Arthrospores abundant. 6. $ Cystoderma jasonis
10,0 $ Stipe apex violet or purple. Basidiospores 6-7.5 x 3.5-4 µm, oblong to fusiform. 7. $ Cystoderma lilacipes
10,0 $ Pileus brownish ochre. Basidiospores 5.5-7.5 x 2.5-4 µm, oblong to fusiform. 9. $ Cystoderma saarenoksae
11,0 $ Basidiocarp white. Basidiospores 4-5.5 x 2.5-3 µm, ellipsoid to oblong. 13. $ Cystodermella ambrosii
11,12 $ Basidiocarp eoloured
12,0 $ Pileus with différent shade of brown. Basidiospores 3.5-4 x 2-2.5 µm. oblong. 14. $ Cystodermella grantilosa
12,13 $ Pileus brownish orange or red
13,0 $ Cheilocystidia absent. Basidiospores 4-5 x 2-2.5 µm, ellipsoid to oblong.12. $ Cystodermella adnatifolia
13,0 $ Cheilocystidia présent. Basidiospores 3.5-4 x 2-2.5 µm, ellipsoid to oblong.15. $ Cystodermella cinnaburina

